WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.647
1. Go to Contracts and click Add contract.

2
00:00:02.647 --> 00:00:10.943
2. Choose the Supplier, the Agreement type, then the Category: its Family, then Category, and a Subcategory if you like (or type a word to find it). Supplier not there yet? Click Add new supplier.

3
00:00:10.943 --> 00:00:14.483
3. The Title fills in from them as Supplier_Agreement type_What it covers, so every title follows the same pattern. If your admin lets people type their own, you can type over it.

4
00:00:14.483 --> 00:00:19.586
4. Add the value, dates and notice period if you know them. A draft only needs enough for its title; the rest is checked when you send it on.

5
00:00:19.586 --> 00:00:22.348
5. Leave Needs Legal review ticked unless Legal has agreed it doesn't need one.

6
00:00:22.348 --> 00:00:28.043
6. Click Save draft. The contract gets its reference, for example JBSAUS0000416.
